2. RetryConfig — change the 4xx logging

You already have the correct retry behavior:

return statusCode >= 500 && statusCode < 600;

So 400 is not retried. Good.

But this code is still wrong for the story:

log.error(new LogBuilder()
        .withMessage("Is this request retryable?")
        .withField("statusCode", statusCode)
        .toString());

For a 400, you're still generating an ERROR log.

Change it to

public boolean isRetryable(Throwable throwable) {
    if (throwable instanceof WebClientResponseException ex) {
        int statusCode = ex.getStatusCode().value();

        log.debug(
                new LogBuilder()
                        .withMessage("Evaluating SendFlex request retry")
                        .withField("statusCode", statusCode)
                        .toString());

        return statusCode >= 500 && statusCode < 600;
    }

    return true;
}

You could also remove the log entirely. I actually prefer removing it unless it is useful operationally.

For example:

public boolean isRetryable(Throwable throwable) {
    if (throwable instanceof WebClientResponseException ex) {
        int statusCode = ex.getStatusCode().value();
        return statusCode >= 500 && statusCode < 600;
    }

    return true;
}

I recommend the second version.


