5. Add a separate persistence method

Do not modify your existing:

persistAddressValidationFailure()

because that method correctly marks genuine failures as:

.statusCode(FAILURE)

Instead add:

private SendFlexRecordDto persistAddressValidationValidationFailure(
    AddressValidationRequestDTO addressValidationRequestDTO,
    ValidationException exception) {

    SendFlexRecordDto sendFlexRecordDto =
        SendFlexRecordDto.builder()
            .requestObject(addressValidationRequestDTO)
            .responseObject(exception.getMessage())
            .statusCode(null)
            .apiCode(ServiceCommonConstants.ADDRESS_VALIDATION_ENDPOINT)
            .build();

    return sendFlexRecordUtil.saveSendflexRecord(sendFlexRecordDto);
}

This is the part that satisfies:

> If we mark the errors as NULL, then the errors will not appear in the alert dashboard.



So your records become:

Expected address validation error

statusCode = null

Actual technical failure

statusCode = failure

That's the separation we want.


